-- title:
--   Extra level at ℓ is preserved exactly on Γ∩ sΓ s⁻¹
-- statement:
--   Numerical data. Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r\neq r$, a nonzero natural number $N$ and a natural number $n$ are given, subject to: $r\nmid N$, $\bar r\nmid N$, $N$ squarefree, $3\le n$, $r\nmid n$, $\bar r\nmid n$, and $n$ coprime to $N$.
--
--   Coefficient rings. $\mathcal{O}$ is a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi\in\mathcal{O}$ is irreducible, $\mathcal{O}$ is $\pi$-adically complete, the residue ring $\mathcal{O}/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements, and $(r)=(\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal{O}$; $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero field which is a fraction field of $\mathcal{O}$. Further, $\mathrm{Onr}$ is a characteristic-zero domain and $\mathcal{O}$-algebra which is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal being maximal, such that every element of $\mathrm{Onr}$ satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}$ modulo that ideal (`hOnr_alg`) and every monic polynomial over $\mathrm{Onr}$ of positive degree has a root modulo that ideal (`hOnr_closed`). The base ring for all moduli below is the residue ring $k_0=\mathrm{Onr}/(\pi)$.
--
--   Quaternion data. $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ satisfies `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b r rbar`: $0<a$ or $0<b$, and the completion at a finite place is a division algebra exactly at the places above $r$ and $\bar r$. $\Lambda$ is a maximal order in it (`IsMaximalOrder`: an order maximal among orders) containing the image of $\mathbb{Z}$, and $\mathrm{coord}:\Lambda\to\mathbb{Z}_{r^2}\times\mathbb{Z}_{r^2}$, with $\mathbb{Z}_{r^2}=W(\mathbb{F}_{r^2})$, satisfies `IsOrderCoord`: it is additive, sends $1$ to $(1,0)$, is multiplicative for the twisted law built from multiplication, $r$ and the Witt Frobenius, is injective, has dense image modulo every power of $r$, and matches reduced traces in the first coordinate.
--
--   The definite algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ satisfies `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt rbar`: $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$, and its completion is a division algebra exactly at the places above $\bar r$. In it, $\Lambda_1$ is a maximal order, $R_1\le\Lambda_1$ is an Eichler order of level $N$ (an intersection of two maximal orders of relative index $N$ in one of them), $\iota_0$ is an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map into $M_2(K_0)$, $v$ is a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ containing $r$, and $\Gamma_t$ is a subgroup of the unit group whose elements are exactly those of `awayUnits R₁ v`, the units lying in the local unit box of $R_1$ at every height-one prime other than $v$.
--
--   Moduli and formal data. $A_0$ is a fake elliptic curve of type $(\Lambda,N)$ over $k_0$, $X_0$ is a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over $k_0$ for the prime $r$ with `HasHeight 4`, $\theta_0$ is a system of formal coordinates of dimension $2$ for $A_0.f$, and `hA₀` asserts `IsFormalModuleVia coord X₀ θ₀`: $\theta_0$ is a formal coordinate system for the group law $A_0.L$ with formal group $X_0.F$, and the action of $m\in\Lambda$ on points is computed on infinitesimal coordinates by the series $\mathrm{act}(\mathrm{coord}(m)_1)$ added to $\mathrm{act}(\mathrm{coord}(m)_2)\circ\varpi$.
--
--   The dictionary on $\Gamma_t$. Families $e,e':\Gamma_t\to\mathrm{End}(A_0.A)$ are given with $e\gamma$ over $A_0.f$ (`he`), together with $\deg:\Gamma_t\to\mathbb{N}$ and the following hypotheses. `hE1`: each pair $(e\gamma,e'\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ on $A_0$ (additive on points in both directions, commuting with the $\Lambda$-action, with both composites equal to multiplication by $r^{\deg\gamma}$) and $e\gamma$ preserves the level structure $A_0.\mathrm{lev}$. `hE1mul`: $e(\gamma\gamma')$ agrees with $e\gamma'$ followed by $e\gamma$ after composing each side with multiplication by a suitable power of $r$. `hE1sc`: if $\gamma$ is the scalar $c\in\mathbb{Z}$ then $e\gamma$ composed with multiplication by $r^i$ is multiplication by $cr^i$ for some $i$. `hE1'`: conversely, if $e\gamma$ becomes multiplication by a positive integer after composing with a power of $r$, then $\gamma$ is a rational scalar. `hE2`: for every injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the actions and of $\varpi$ in $\mathrm{End}(X_0.F)$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that every $\gamma$ admits $\varepsilon$ in that centraliser and $k_\gamma\in\mathbb{Z}$ with $\varepsilon$ inducing $e\gamma$ on all infinitesimal coordinates (the displayed truncated-evaluation identity for every $k_0$-algebra $B'$, every ideal $J$ with $J^{m+1}=0$ and every $s$ with entries in $J$) and $E_0\varepsilon=r^{k_\gamma}\,g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$. `hE3`: every full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$ admits a labelling $\mathrm{lab}:\Gamma_t\to\Lambda$ with $e\gamma$ acting on $P_0$ as $\mathrm{lab}\,\gamma$, multiplicative modulo $n\Lambda$, and sending scalars $c$ to $c$ modulo $n\Lambda$. `hE4`: for every algebraically closed field $k$ over $k_0$, every fake elliptic curve $A$ over $k$ and every $g_A:A.A\to A_0.A$ exhibiting $A$ as the pullback of $A_0$ along $k_0\to k$, every level-preserving isogeny pair on $A$ of degree a power of $r$ is, after composing with suitable powers of $r$, carried by $g_A$ into some $e\gamma$.
--
--   The dictionary on orders. $R_2\le R_1$ is an order such that every element of $R_1$ becomes an element of $R_2$ after multiplication by a power of $r$, and $\hat e:R_2\to\mathrm{End}(A_0.A)$ lies over $A_0.f$. The hypotheses `hE5a` (additivity on points, commutation with the $\Lambda$-action, preservation of $A_0.\mathrm{lev}$), `hE5one`, `hE5mul`, `hE5int`, `hE5c` ($\hat e(\bar x)$ followed by $\hat e(x)$ is multiplication by $\mathrm{nrd}(x)$), `hE5d` (compatibility of $\hat e$ with $e\gamma$ on $r$-power multiples of $\gamma$ up to powers of $r$), `hE5e` (the dictionary of `hE2` extended, with a single conjugator $g$, to all $x\in R_2$ with $\iota_0(x)$ in place of $\iota_0(\gamma)$) and `hE5g` ($R_2$ is stable under the main involution) are imposed.
--
--   Twin order and a second dictionary. $\Lambda_{1s}$ is a maximal order with $R_1\le\Lambda_{1s}$ and $\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_{1s}=R_1$; $R_2'\le\Lambda_{1s}$ is an order with $R_2\le R_2'$ such that every element of $\Lambda_{1s}$ lies in $R_2'$ after multiplication by a power of $r$; and $\hat e':R_2'\to\mathrm{End}(A_0.A)$ lies over $A_0.f$ and satisfies `hE6a` (additivity on points and commutation with the $\Lambda$-action), `hE6one`, `hE6mul`, `hE6int`, `hE6c`, `hE6d` ($\hat e'$ restricts to $\hat e$ on $R_2$), `hE6star`, `hE6inj` (injectivity of $\hat e'$) and `hE6f`: for every prime $q\neq r$ and every $z\in R_2'$, if $\hat e'(z)$ annihilates all $q$-torsion points, then $r^Kz=qy$ for some $K$ and some $y\in\Lambda_{1s}$.
--
--   Hecke data. $n_1$ is a finite-adelic unit in `primeHeckeSet R₁ r`, with `meetOrder R₁ n₁` an Eichler order of level $Nr$; $\ell$ is a prime different from $r$ and $\bar r$; $s$ is a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ and $s_f$ a finite-adelic unit, and `hs` requires: $s_f$ equals $s\otimes 1$ at every height-one prime not containing $r$, equals $1$ at the primes containing $r$, the product of the diagonal image of $\ell$ with $s_f^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` when $\ell\mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s)=\ell$.
--
--   The extra level and its isogeny. $C_0$ is an `ExtraLevel` structure of order $\ell$ on $A_0$: a closed immersion $C_0.\mathrm{levK}$ into $A_0.A$ whose points form a $\Lambda$-stable subgroup of $\ell$-torsion points, disjoint from $A_0.\mathrm{lev}$, finite flat of finite presentation of rank $\ell^2$ over the base, with geometric fibres isomorphic as groups to $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^2$. Further, $A_{0s}$ is a fake elliptic curve over $k_0$, $a_s:A_0.A\to A_{0s}.A$ and $a_s'$ in the other direction lie over the structure maps, $k_s\in\mathbb{N}$, $b_s:A_{0s}.A\to A_0.A$ and $b_s'$ lie over the structure maps, and: `hCs` says $(a_s,a_s')$ is a level-$\ell$ isogeny from $(A_0,C_0)$ to $A_{0s}$, in particular a point is killed by $a_s$ exactly when it factors through $C_0.\mathrm{levK}$; `hbsI` says $(b_s,b_s')$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_s}$; `hbsL` says $b_s$ preserves the level; `hH2s` is the joint formal dictionary asserting, for every injective $E_0$ as above, the existence of one $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ serving simultaneously for all $\gamma\in\Gamma_t$ as in `hE2` and for the composite $a_s$ followed by $b_s$, with $\iota_0(\bar s)$ in place of $\iota_0(\gamma)$. Finally $m_s\in\mathbb{N}$ satisfies $r^{m_s}\bar s\in R_2$ and `hH3s` asserts the morphism-level identity that $a_s$ followed by $b_s$ equals $\hat e\big(r^{m_s}\bar s\big)$.
--
--   Conclusion. For every $\gamma\in\Gamma_t$ the following two assertions are equivalent:
--
--   (i) for every scheme $T$, every morphism $t$ from $T$ to the spectrum of $k_0$ and every point $P$ of $A_0$ over $t$, if $P$ factors through $C_0.\mathrm{levK}$ then the image of $P$ under $e\gamma$ factors through $C_0.\mathrm{levK}$; that is, $e\gamma$ maps the extra level $C_0$ into itself on all points;
--
--   (ii) $\gamma$ lies in $\Gamma_t\sqcap\Gamma_t.\mathrm{map}(\mathrm{conj}\,s)$, the intersection of $\Gamma_t$ with its conjugate $s\Gamma_ts^{-1}$.
--
--   This is the stabiliser computation in the dictionary between the Čerednik–Drinfel'd side and the definite quaternion side: it identifies the elements of the dictionary group $\Gamma_t$ whose associated endomorphism of the fake elliptic curve $A_0$ respects the auxiliary level-$\ell$ subgroup scheme $C_0$ as exactly the intersection of $\Gamma_t$ with the conjugate $s\Gamma_ts^{-1}$, where $s$ is the quaternion of reduced norm $\ell$ whose dictionary endomorphism has kernel containing $C_0$. It is used in the construction of the Čerednik–Drinfel'd tower of fine moduli data, where the raised-level group $\Gamma_t\cap s\Gamma_ts^{-1}$ is the one attached to level $N\ell$. The proof quotes the two coset-graph lemmas describing `awayUnits` by $r$-power denominators and giving membership in the conjugated group.
